Solar is now the cheapest source of electricity ever built — IRENA's 2022 report found that 86% of new renewable capacity added in 2021 had lower costs than the cheapest fossil fuel alternatives.
The renewable energy sector employed 12.7 million people worldwide in 2023, up from 7.3 million in 2012, making it one of the fastest-growing employment sectors globally.
Every dollar invested in clean energy produces 3× more jobs than the equivalent investment in fossil fuels, according to a 2021 analysis published in Nature Climate Change.
US clean energy jobs (4 million in 2023) already outnumber fossil fuel jobs by 3:1, and are growing 3× faster than the overall economy.
